        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "d526ee90-8530-5da8-ad8b-ec5016bff167",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Garth Richardson, Jack Richardson, Pete Ham, Ron Griffiths, David \"Dai\" Jenkins\n- Bands: Badfinger, The Iveys, Daughters of Mara, Jellyfish\n- Companies: Virgin Records\n- Songs/Albums: I Am Destroyer, \"No Matter What\"\n\nFacts:\n- In 1961, Pete Ham, Ron Griffiths, and David \"Dai\" Jenkins formed The Iveys in Swansea, Wales.\n- Badfinger evolved from the earlier band The Iveys.\n- Jack Richardson was a Canadian music producer whose credits included Alice Cooper, The Guess Who, Badfinger, and Poco.\n- Garth Richardson is the son of Canadian music producer Jack Richardson.\n- Daughters of Mara's first album, I Am Destroyer, was produced by Garth Richardson and released on Virgin Records.\n- On Jellyfish's album Best!, the song \"No Matter What\" is a live cover of a Badfinger song.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "59c9b83c-b49b-5aec-b24f-9a800a4b19b7",
        "text": "Page: Garth Richardson. Sentence: He is the son of Canadian music producer Jack Richardson (whose credits include Alice Cooper, The Guess Who, Badfinger and Poco).\nPage: Badfinger. Sentence: The band evolved from an earlier group called The Iveys that was formed in 1961 by Ham, Ron Griffiths and David \"Dai\" Jenkins in Swansea, Wales.\nPage: Daughters of Mara. Sentence: Daughters Of Mara's first album, I Am Destroyer, was produced by Garth Richardson (Mudvayne, Rage Against The Machine) and was released on Virgin Records.\nPage: Best! (Jellyfish album). Sentence: The song \"No Matter What\" is a live cover of a Badfinger song.",
